<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!--
    SpotBugs exclusions for brat-core.

    EI_EXPOSE_REP / EI_EXPOSE_REP2 - "may expose internal representation" - was excluded as a whole
    family from 2026-08-04 until Phase 7c (2026-08-11), because every one of the nine hits was the
    same open question: whether the data classes should become records, gain defensive copies, or
    lose their setters. That question is now decided and applied - the authored data types are final
    or sealed, hold final fields, copy their collections in, and hand out unmodifiable views - so the
    blanket exclusion is gone and only the three classes below are still listed, each for its own
    stated reason. Anything new that trips this pattern now fails the build, which is the point.

    - SecretsProviderConfig: a false positive. It already copies its maps in the compact
      constructor, which SpotBugs cannot see through.

    - AssertionResult: a record whose `condition` component is a mutable Condition. Fixing it means
      deciding whether a result may hand out the condition it reports on, which belongs with the
      result types being designed in Phase 8a/8b - see flight-plan.md, "RequestResult / outcome
      shape". Listed rather than fixed so the decision is made once, with the rest of them.

    - RenderTarget: the same shape one layer out, in api.rendering. It is a plugin-facing contract,
      so changing what it hands a renderer is an API decision rather than a cleanup; it belongs with
      the reporter-layer work rather than here.
-->
<FindBugsFilter>
    <Match>
        <Class name="dev.pbroman.brat.core.secrets.SecretsProviderConfig"/>
        <Bug pattern="EI_EXPOSE_REP,EI_EXPOSE_REP2"/>
    </Match>
    <Match>
        <Class name="dev.pbroman.brat.core.data.result.AssertionResult"/>
        <Bug pattern="EI_EXPOSE_REP,EI_EXPOSE_REP2"/>
    </Match>
    <Match>
        <Class name="dev.pbroman.brat.core.api.rendering.RenderTarget"/>
        <Bug pattern="EI_EXPOSE_REP,EI_EXPOSE_REP2"/>
    </Match>
</FindBugsFilter>
